I don't think you are calling the [`ShouldSerialize`](https://www.newtonsoft.com/json/help/html/P_Newtonsoft_Json_Serialization_JsonProperty_ShouldSerialize.htm) predicate correctly.  It takes an *instance of the containing object* not the *property value*, and so should never get called with `null`.  Thus you should call it like so:

    contractProperty.ShouldSerialize.Invoke(new SomeClass());

As [`ShouldSerialize`](https://www.newtonsoft.com/json/help/html/ConditionalProperties.htm#ShouldSerialize) is intended to be an [open delegate](https://blog.slaks.net/2011/06/open-delegates-vs-closed-delegates.html) encapsulating the standard [`ShouldSerializeXXX`](https://stackoverflow.com/q/37838640/3744182) instance method, the first (and only) argument to the predicate is the instance itself.

