I've fixed this with a new setting called `EncodeSpecialCharacters`.

```cs
const string initialJson = @"{""Be:fore:After!"":""Value!""}";

XDocument xmlNode = JsonConvert.DeserializeXNode(initialJson, null, false, encodeSpecialCharacters: true);

Assert.AreEqual("<Be_x003A_fore_x003A_After_x0021_>Value!</Be_x003A_fore_x003A_After_x0021_>", xmlNode.ToString());

string json = JsonConvert.SerializeXNode(xmlNode);

Assert.AreEqual(initialJson, json);
```
When it is set to true, all special characters in JSON property names are encoded into the XML element name instead of indicating specify XML semantics.

